<header><p class="st-kicker">khanate · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Tyumen Khanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1405 CE – 1495 CE (approx.) · capital Chimgi-Tura</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Shibanid khanate of western Siberia that briefly ruled the Golden Horde's eastern steppes and was the forerunner of the Khanate of Sibir.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Tyumen Khanate grew from the old <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ulus-of-shiban">Ulus of Shiban</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyumen">Chimgi-Tura</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tura-river">Tura River</a> in the early 15th century, as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> authority faded. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaybanids">Shibanid</a> princes ruled there, and the khan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abul-khayr-khan">Abu'l-Khayr</a> was proclaimed in this region in 1428 before moving south.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The khanate ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatar</a> nomads and the forest peoples of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a>, collecting tribute in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">furs</a> that were traded south and west. Its most notable ruler, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibak-khan">Ibak Khan</a>, took part in the destruction of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/great-horde">Great Horde</a>, killing its khan Ahmad in 1481 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-stand-on-the-ugra-river">Great Stand on the Ugra River</a>, and claimed leadership among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jochids">Jochids</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 1495 the local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taibugids">Taibugid</a> clan seized power, killing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibak-khan">Ibak</a> and moving the capital to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qashliq">Qashliq</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irtysh">Irtysh</a>, founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khanate-of-sibir">Khanate of Sibir</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyumen">Chimgi-Tura</a> was later rebuilt by the Russians as Tyumen in 1586.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="khanate, 1405 CE – 1495 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 74 V58 Q50 30 82 58 V74 Z"/><path d="M42 74 V60 H58 V74"/><path d="M30 50 L50 36 L70 50"/><path d="M50 36 V26"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">khanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central Asia and the Steppe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:87.66%;width:1.79%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1405 CE – 1495 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>khanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Chimgi-Tura</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ibak Khan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam, Tengrism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Siberian Tatar</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Chimgi-Tura Khanate</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1450&amp;focus=tyumen-khanate" aria-label="Tyumen Khanate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6089 240 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Tyumen Khanate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6409 496L6352 637M6409 496L6409 496M6409 496L6439 487"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6352 637h0M6409 496h0M6439 487h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6409 496h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6409 496h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Chimgi-Tura. <a href="/atlas?year=1450&amp;focus=tyumen-khanate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
